comments[14]{created_at,author,text}:
  "2026-11-26T10:25:17.260Z",codex-agent,"Imported issue 286 through the pinned CLI. Reproducing the released atomic gated comment mirror in an isolated clone, then checking the reserved-ID refusal through the shared import ownership guard."
  "2026-11-26T10:27:00.950Z",codex-agent,"Reproduced with locked pm CLI 2026.11.24 and pm-github 2026.11.25 on the clean public pm-rl main at 273a687: comments 17 to 18 to 19. The second import reported zero item updates yet changed the tracker. The SDK comments read shortened the stored 1221-character bot comment to 253 characters, hiding its trailing stable ID; the persisted item still had the full marker. Removing the explicit link in the isolated fixture also reproduced github_import_owner_conflict without a copyable repair."
  "2026-11-26T10:29:16.576Z",codex-agent,"Control confirmed on pm-ado main at ce4b8c1: issue 137 comments 5 to 6 to 6, with identical item bytes on repeat. Its SDK list retained all 1079 characters and the trailing ID. The defect depends on SDK output compaction, not on comment count or timestamps alone. The same bounded read feeds blocker-comment marker detection, so both consumers now read the native annotation store."
  "2026-11-26T10:33:05.885Z",codex-agent,"The first packed fixed replay on pristine pm-rl main produced 17 to 18 to 18. The GitHub bot row retained 2026-11-24T18:15:04Z. Item and history bytes matched after each repeat, which reported unchanged and passed the same gate. Reserved-ID guidance is restricted to an unowned creation destination, with the usable command carried through the typed diagnostic."
  "2026-11-26T10:40:09.744Z",codex-agent,"Behavioral reverts were rebuilt in a disposable copy. Restoring the old comment sync and removing the reserved-ID guidance and issue-start help failed four regressions: byte-identical repeat, native mirror behavior, the JSON/TOON repair and help. Reverting only the timestamp factory failed with import time in place of 2026-01-01T03:04:05Z. Restoring only the bounded blocker read failed the no-Git grouped marker preview/apply regression. All five pass with the fixes restored. The linked pm test command passed."
  "2026-11-26T10:47:48.014Z",codex-agent,"The packed candidate passed the two-import check through npx --no-install pm and bunx --bun --no-install pm, with locked host 2026.11.24 and the captured public REST and read-only GraphQL responses. Both repeated imports reported unchanged, zero imports and updates, passed the gate and left item and history bytes identical. The independent packed minimum-SDK consumer test passed 1/1 at 2026.10.23. All six focused Node regressions passed."
  "2026-11-26T11:28:54.769Z",codex-agent,"The targeted 57-file Node run completed with 1445 passing tests, no failures and no skips. Typecheck, test compilation, lint, the 323-declaration docstring gate, the 34-module duplication gate, and the ownership inventory all passed. The staged privacy scan audited 10590 objects and found no unapproved identities, credentials or host paths."
  "2026-11-26T11:31:25.047Z",codex-agent,Final comment-path recheck passed 26/26. Returning this item to open and releasing the claim for exact-head CI handoff. CI coverage and release checks remain at the repository thresholds. CI monitoring is capped at 30 minutes from the last push.
  "2026-11-26T12:45:53.885Z",pi-glm,"Re-review round 1 blocked the PR with three findings; continuing on the same branch, PR and item. Plan per finding, closing the class not the line:\n\n1. Repair command without the failing invocation's tracker selector (import-repair): general rule - a rendered repair command must replay the caller's tracker scope, like the host's revision-recovery scopeArgs. Fix: the reserved-ID repair command includes the tracker selector the failed import used, so copying it from any directory updates only that tracker. Search: every rendered repair/example command in the package that writes to a tracker item gets the same scope treatment.\n\n2. Repair offered on incomplete provenance (import-repair): general rule - a repair is offered only when applying it leaves exactly one consistent GitHub owner, evaluated with the same ownership-claims machinery the next import uses. Fix: the refusal carries the refused item snapshot and the offer is withheld unless the post-link claims are exactly the target issue. Search: every other adoption/link suggestion for the same precondition.\n\n3. Comment mirror stores source timestamps unvalidated (comment-mirror): general rule - external source timestamps are validated before persistence, like the importer's source-lifetime gate; a malformed value must count as a failed write and stay retryable, never be stored and skipped by marker. Search: every other path that persists source-provided timestamps.\n\nNon-blocking CodeRabbit out-of-scope check: factually wrong - the comment-mirror requirements are stated in issue #286's first comment (the non-convergent linked-item mirror), which this PR fixes alongside the reserved-ID refusal by design; the suggested alternative (link an issue that states the comment requirements) is already satisfied by that comment. Will strengthen the PR body's explicit link to it."
  "2026-11-26T13:14:32.834Z",pi-glm,"Round-1 blocking findings implemented on the same branch; no second PR, no new item.\n\n1. Scope replay: a new invocation scope (AsyncLocalStorage, same pattern the host uses for its own recovery scope) captures the typed tracker selector at the four command registrations that can render invocation-bound commands (github/gh-issues import, refresh, webhooks reconcile). The reserved-ID repair now renders pm --pm-path <the failing invocation's own spelling> update <id> --field github_url=<url>, matching the host's revision-recovery convention: replay the typed selector verbatim, keep an implicit (cwd/PM_PATH) selection implicit so a same-shell copy resolves the same tracker. Class search found two more invocation-bound rendered commands and fixed both the same way: the comment-mirror ownership-conflict release example (comment-mirror.ts) and the webhook reconcile recovery hint (webhooks.ts).\n\n2. Safe-link predicate: the curated/unowned refusal now carries the refused item snapshot non-enumerably (never serialized into diagnostics), and the link offer is kept only when the item's post-link ownership claims are exactly the target issue, evaluated with the same githubOwnershipClaims the next import uses. A reserved item with a contradicting github_number or github_repo keeps the plain refusal, so the offered repair can never create contradictory ownership that blocks the next import.\n\n3. Timestamp validation: the mirror validates each source comment timestamp before any write; a missing or unparseable one is counted failed and retried on the next sync, never stored and never skipped by its marker id. Item-level source lifetimes already had this rule (validateImportLifetime); the comment mirror was the one unvalidated persistence path in the package."
  "2026-11-26T14:44:39.106Z",pi-glm,"Revert proofs (behavioral reverts in a disposable copy, restored and re-verified green after each):\n\n- Scope revert: rendering the repair without the invocation's selector failed the tracker-scoped regression at the first assertion, with the refusal showing the bare pm update command. Restored: pass.\n- Provenance revert: dropping the post-link claims predicate made the refusal offer the link to the item carrying github_number=8, failing 'a link that would create contradictory ownership must not be offered'. Restored: pass.\n- Timestamp revert: storing comment.created_at unvalidated counted the three malformed comments as added=4/failed=0 and wrote malformed rows, failing the deep-equal. Restored: pass.\n- With all fixes restored the full linked-import regression file passes 8/8 in the disposable copy.\n\nOne existing fixture needed its comment timestamp made valid, not a weakened assertion: coverage-remainder's metadata-preservation and read-only-directory tests used created_at empty strings as don't-care values; each now carries a valid source timestamp so the same write paths are still exercised (the read-only failure still fails at the write; the metadata row still lands). The body-mode builder tests keep their empty timestamps because body text is mirrored content, not persisted metadata.\n\nGates so far: typecheck, build, test build, lint, docstring (328 declarations), duplication (34 modules, zero clones), privacy (10654 objects audited), the ownership inventory regenerated and verified (one new classified group for the repair renderer), and the packed minimum-SDK consumer (2026.10.23) passed. Focused regressions: linked-import 8/8; comments-sync/import-ownership/ownership-consistency/import-errors/scoped-ownership 208; webhooks/workflow-diagnostic/cited-adoption/import-lock/legacy-description/owner-field-values 121; round-seventeen/eighteen/twelve/sdk-adoption 41; coverage-remainder 25; identity-inventory 9; coverage-edges 9; minimum-sdk 1. A full 100-file local run was stopped at the 90-minute mark after an npm EALLOWSCRIPTS flake in strict-import-admission under two-worker concurrency; that file passes 2/2 standalone and unchanged thresholds remain for CI."
  "2026-11-26T14:50:29.390Z",pi-glm,"Class closure beyond the named line, with two more surfaces found by the same rule search and their own revert proofs:\n\n- The comment mirror's ownership-conflict release guidance (comment-mirror.ts) also rendered an unscoped 'pm release <id>' example; it now replays the failing invocation's selector, verified by a strict-governance held-item test that fails on the unscoped revert.\n- The webhook reconcile recovery hint (webhooks.ts) rendered an unscoped 'pm github refresh <repo> --dry-run'; it now replays the selector, verified by a reconcile test asserting both the scoped and implicit forms, failing on the unscoped revert.\n\nBoth revert proofs ran in a disposable copy; with the fixes restored, the linked-import and webhook files pass 22/22, and the ownership inventory, lint, docstring (328 declarations) and duplication gates (zero clones, 34 modules) all re-passed after the additions."
  "2026-11-26T15:18:14.215Z",pi-glm,"Exact-head CI is green on the pushed head: both test matrix legs passed (13m and 24m), codeql, CodeQL, semgrep and Greptile passed; CodeRabbit, Sourcery and cubic skipped on review budgets, and the auto-merge and armed-request gates hold their usual skip state pending the merge decision. Coverage and release gates stay at unchanged thresholds, certified by CI. The PR body now links the issue's first comment explicitly for the out-of-scope check and names the three round-1 fixes. Returning the item to open; the claim is released for the orchestrator's verification."
  "2026-11-26T15:44:01.425Z",pi-glm,"At the 30-minute cutoff after the last push (tracker-only commit 1066569), test (22) passed in 16m44s and the slow matrix leg is still running: https://github.com/unbraind/pm-github/actions/runs/45847787395 (job 140005865970). The identical code at head f0c326c passed both legs (13m11s and 24m12s) plus codeql, CodeQL, semgrep and Greptile; only the .agents/pm tracker files differ on the new head. Stopping per the CI-wait cap; the pending URL is also in the final report."
